ailable":"This block's direct messages are no longer in the session (pruned by native compaction) \u2014 their m-refs cannot be listed","det.tree_msg_gone":"This message is no longer in the session (pruned by native compaction)","det.tree_hint":"Nested by fold parent: T1 folds raw messages, T2 folds T1 blocks, and so on. Original loads the covered bytes on demand.","det.tree_view_list":"List","det.tree_view_graph":"Tree map","det.tree_graph_hint":"Overall shape: each box is one block, top-down is which block folded which. Click a box to jump to that row in the list.","det.tree_graph_legend":"solid border = active, dashed = archived","det.handoff":"Handoff document","det.handoff_hint":"Same content as bili export \u2014 paste into a new session to continue","det.thinking":"thinking","det.handoff_truncated":"\u26A0\uFE0F Content truncated for display","det.handoff_copy_md":"Copy as Markdown","det.handoff_download":"Download .md","det.not_found":"Session not found","det.not_found_hint":"It may have been deleted or lives outside this data dir","cfg.title":"Configuration","cfg.sub":"Edits write straight to the config file and hot-apply \xB7 check JSON syntax before saving","cfg.file":"Config file","cfg.parse_error":"Config file is not valid JSON \u2014 showing an empty view","cfg.relay_warn":"The draft enables security.adminRelay (admin relay): anyone who can reach the dsh web entry gets the FULL bili admin panel through it \u2014 including config edits and credential writes. Make sure that entry is behind login auth or a reverse proxy; remove the field to turn it back off.","cfg.upstream_net":"Upstream network","cfg.up_auto":"auto (follow system proxy)","cfg.up_manual":"manual (explicit proxy)","cfg.up_direct":"direct (force direct)","cfg.passthrough":"Passthrough","cfg.passthrough_desc":"Decides whether traffic matching no route passes through to the target service untouched (no interception, no rewriting). State lives in the config file; when forced by the ACP_PASSTHROUGH env var the UI marks the source and you must unset the variable and restart before changing it here","cfg.pt_off":"Off","cfg.pt_on":"On","cfg.test_hint":"Sends one minimal request to verify reachability; changes nothing","cfg.test_btn":"Test connection","cfg.state":"Connection state","cfg.untested":"Not probed yet","cfg.save":"Save","cfg.unsaved":"\u26A0 Unsaved changes \u2014 nothing is written until you click Save","cfg.file_desc":"This card edits the config file directly \u2014 every top-level field in this JSON takes effect (routes, compression, network, passthrough, promptPack, ccr, \u2026). Saving applies immediately","cfg.quick":"Quick settings","cfg.quick_desc":"Toggle common options without touching JSON \u2014 every change syncs live into the raw editor below (same file, no new config fields); advanced structures like the providers table stay in the JSON","cfg.q_debug":"Debug logging (debug)","cfg.q_passthrough":"Passthrough mode (passthrough) \u2014 pure proxying, no injection, no compression","cfg.q_imgrescale":"Outbound image downscale (imageRescale) \u2014 large outbound images are shrunken before reaching the model; originals stay in local session storage (default on)","cfg.q_imgrescale_hint":"longest-edge threshold via env BILI_IMAGE_RESCALE_MAX_DIM (default 1600)","cfg.q_absorb":"Instant tool-result absorption (absorb) \u2014 large tool results are distilled by the model on arrival; originals hidden until the next fold round (default off)","cfg.q_absorb_hint":"by default only image-bearing results are absorbed (#3422); set mediaOnly: false to absorb full text. Sub-fields (minToolTokens, contextThresholdPct, excludeTools) go in the JSON editor below","cfg.q_pack":"Compression prompt pack (compress.promptPack)","cfg.q_nudge":"Compress growth threshold tokens (compress.nudgeGrowthTokens)","cfg.q_nudge_step":"step of 5000","cfg.q_nudge_low":"below 20000: folding this often degrades summary quality (kernel default 50000)","cfg.q_nudge_high":"above 1