--passthrough flag)","sys.pt_file":"config file passthrough: true","sys.storage_degraded_title":"SQLite storage degraded:","sys.storage_degraded":"Unified SQLite storage becomes the default in an upcoming release, but this system cannot run it ({reason}). You have been automatically rolled back to JSON storage \u2014 nothing is affected today. Please report this so your environment is covered before the flip.","sys.snapshot_shadow_title":"Snapshot render shadow found mismatches","sys.snapshot_shadow":"The outbound snapshot engine (not enabled yet \u2014 shadow-compare only) found {n} mismatches against what was actually sent{worst}. Nothing you send is affected today \u2014 this is a pre-rollout health check alarm. Please report the diagnostics so it can be fixed before the flip.","sys.report_copy":"Copy diagnostics","sys.report_issue":"Report on GitHub","conflict.on":"Compression conflict detected","conflict.found":": traces of ","conflict.what_plugin":"a third-party compression plugin co-resident with bili","conflict.what_native":"client-native auto-compaction rewriting conversation history","conflict.what_join":" and ","conflict.risk_active":" were found. Two compressors on one conversation double-compress and corrupt message refs, which can scramble context \u2014 keep exactly one compressor.","conflict.risk_sibling":" were found. These are bili's OWN sibling extensions, not third-party compressors: while bili drives the session they stand down automatically (BILLION_CONTEXT_NATIVE marker in native mode, /bili/ baseUrl self-check otherwise), so no second compressor is active \u2014 verify your versions are recent and clear this record; nothing needs removing.","conflict.risk_historical":" were found (no events in the last 7 days \u2014 stock records only) \u2014 once you've confirmed the other compressor is removed or blocked by bili, clear them with the button.","conflict.on_suspected":"Possible compression plugin detected","conflict.what_suspected":"a plugin whose name matches compression keywords (not yet verified to actually compress context)","conflict.risk_suspected":" \u2014 a name-only [suspected] signal, not observed evidence of double-compression. Confirm it actually rewrites the model context before acting; a display / tool-output-folding plugin (e.g. pi-compact-transcript) does not double-compress and needs no removal.","conflict.on_unconfirmed":"Unconfirmed compression-related signals detected","conflict.what_signal":"conversation history being rewritten (a change was observed, cause not yet identified)","conflict.risk_unconfirmed":" \u2014 all of the above are UNCONFIRMED signals: they do not prove a second compressor exists (possible causes: client-side edits, an unrecognized compaction shape, or another plugin). Verify before acting; a read-only context viewer or a display / tool-output-folding plugin is not a compressor and needs no removal.","conflict.age_active":"{n} in last 7 days","conflict.age_historical":"{n} older","conflict.where":"Details: Sessions page below or the conflicts field of GET /__bili/stats.","conflict.clear_btn":"Clear records","conflict.cleared":"Conflict records cleared","conflict.dismiss":"Don't show again","conflict.dismissed":"Dismissed \u2014 the banner re-arms if a new conflict event lands","conflict.hint_label":"What to do (per client):","conflict.hint.opencode":'opencode: set "compaction": { "auto": false } in your opencode config (or use bili opencode / bili plugin install opencode, which set it for you)',"conflict.hint.claude":"claude: launch through bili claude (it aligns CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW automatically), or set CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW to bili's effective window yourself","conflict.hint.codex":"codex: bili intercepts native compaction by default (BILI_CODEX_COMPACT=intercept) \u2014 if you set pass, remove the override to stop; otherwise report your bili version","conflict.hint.pi":"pi: the bili extension cancels the client's native auto-compaction while it carries the conversation \u2014 seeing this suggests missing carriage evidence or an old version; report client + bili version","conflict.hint.omp":"omp: the bili extension cancels the client's native auto-compaction while it carries the conversation \u2014 seeing this suggests missing carriage evidence or an old version; report client + bili version","conflict.hint.generic":"disable the client's own auto-compaction (or route this session around bili), then start a fresh session \u2014 the ledger is per-session, so old entries clear with the old session","conflict.hint_more":"{n} more client(s) \u2014 see the Sessions page below","conflict.docs":'full matrix: CONFIGURATION.md \u2192 "Detecting other compression plugins (#1206)"',"advisory.on":"Critical defect advisory","advisory.desc":": the current version has a major defect; bili is upgrading it automatically to a safe version. Reason:","advisory.hint":". If it did not complete automatically, run manually:","alert.title":"Upstream connection problems","alert.item":"Cannot reach {host} ({kind} \xD7{count}, since {first}) \u2014 {hint}","alert.note.skipped_proxy":'available proxy {proxy} ({source}) was skipped \u2014 upstreamProxyMode is unset (direct is the default by design, #346/#357); set "upstreamProxyMode": "auto" or BILI_UPSTREAM_PROXY_MODE=auto, or give this provider a "proxy" lane to enable it',"alert.dismiss":"Got it","alert.hint.connect_timeout":"TCP handshake never completed \u2014 upstream/proxy unreachable or blackholed; a bounded transparent replay may be attempted (BILI_REPLAY_RETRY_MAX)","alert.hint.connect_refused":"TCP refused (proxy when configured, else upstream) \u2014 endpoint down or wrong port","alert.hint.proxy_reset":"proxy dropped the connection before the response \u2014 check proxy idle-recycle/payload limits (BILI_PROXY_KEEPALIVE_MAX_MS can shorten our reuse window); a bounded transparent replay may be attempted (BILI_REPLAY_RETRY_MAX)","alert.hint.upstream_reset":"upstream/network reset before the response \u2014 check upstream and local network; a bounded transparent replay may be attempted (BILI_REPLAY_RETRY_MAX)","alert.hint.dns":"name resolution failed \u2014 DNS server or hostname typo; a bounded transparent replay may be attempted (BILI_REPLAY_RETRY_MAX)","alert.hint.tls":"TLS/certificate failure at CONNECT or upstream handshake \u2014 CA/proxy MITM config; if the chain is reported untrusted/self-signed, security software doing HTTPS scanning (Kaspersky, enterprise DLP) or a corporate proxy may be re-signing the upstream \u2014 export that root CA to PEM and set NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/path/to/ca.pem (or bili config network.caFile), or exclude node.exe from scanning","alert.hint.unknown":"unclassified transport failure \u2014 report with full error chain","advisory.restartDesc":": the safe version is installed on disk, but this process is still running the affected version. Reason:","advisory.restartHint":". Restart bili to activate it.","hostplug.on":"Host-side plugin detected","hostplug.desc":"Its segment composition / timeline is estimated from the pre-compression local meter (the durable log stays lossless by dsh architecture requirements), so the per-segment proportions may not match what is actually sent; the headline context size tracks the real sent volume.","hostplug.hint":"Authoritative effective context: /acp or GET /__bili/plugin/status \u2192 contextTokens.","hostplug.dismiss_btn":"Dismiss","hostplug.dismissed":"Notice dismissed","pluginadv.on":"High-cost plugin detected","pluginadv.desc":"This plugin re-sends the entire conversation to the model before every tool call for review, so the upstream prefix cache almost never applies (hit rate usually single-digit %) and token cost grows sharply. This is unrelated to bili's compression: bili isolates such requests into a separate sub-session, leaving the main session's prefix cache intact.","pluginadv.hint":"Consider disabling the plugin or asking its maintainers to optimize it; details in the link above (this issue).","pck.on":"Cache routing key (prompt_cache_key) withheld","pck.sessions":"Affected session(s): {ids}","pck.hint":"This upstream rejected requests carrying prompt_cache_key (400 with the key, accepted without it), so bili withholds the key there until restart. If this is your relay/account pool, prefix-cache affinity may degrade for those sessions.","ses.title":"Sessions","ses.sub":"Every session across memory and disk \u2014 click a row for details, trajectory & handoff document","ses.search_ph":"Search title, label or id\u2026","ses.th_title":"Session","ses.th_proto":"Protocol","ses.th_upstream":"Upstream","ses.th_reqs":"Reqs","ses.th_ctx":"Context now","ses.th_saved":"Saved","ses.th_hit":"Hit %","ses.th_switches":"Switches","ses.th_switches_tip":"Mid-session model switches \xB7 tokens re-billed because the new model starts from a cold prefix cache (#1535) \xB7 \u{1F511} = relay key/account rotations (credential fingerprint change, #2131) \xB7 \u270D\uFE0F = host system-prompt rewrites (prompt fingerprint change, #2350) \xB7 \u{1F500} = proxy compression-mode/projection switches (e.g. self-heal degrade-to-proxy, #2867)","ses.th_keyswitches_tip":"Relay key/account rotation (credential fingerprint changed behind the same URL) \xB7 tokens re-billed because the rotated account starts from a cold cache (#2131)","ses.th_promptswitches_tip":"The host rewrote its system prompt (fingerprint changed between requests, e.g. a periodic dynamic section) \xB7 each rewrite invalidates every downstream prefix-cache entry \u2014 tokens re-billed for the stable prefix (#2350)","ses.th_projswitches_tip":"The proxy switched its own compression mode/projection (e.g. self-heal degrade-to-proxy re-hoists mid-history developer messages into the system block) \xB7 each switch invalidates every downstream prefix-cache entry \u2014 tokens re-billed for the stable prefix (#2867)","det.key_events":"Key switches ({n})","det.key_events_tip":"Credential fingerprint change = the relay rotated to a different account; fingerprints are 12-hex sha256 prefixes, never raw keys","det.key_fp":"key fingerprint","det.prompt_events":"System-prompt rewrites ({n})","det.prompt_events_tip":"Forwarded-projection fingerprint change WITH the canonical incoming content also changed = the host rewrote its system prompt between requests; fingerprints are 16-hex sha256 prefixes, never raw text (#2350/#2867)","det.prompt_fp":"prompt fingerprint","det.proj_events":"Projection/mode switches ({n})","det.proj_events_tip":"Forwarded-projection fingerprint changed while the canonical incoming system/developer content stayed identical = the proxy itself switched compression mode/projection (e.g. self-heal degrade-to-proxy); fingerprints are 16-hex sha256 prefixes, never raw text (#2867)","det.proj_fp":"projection fingerprint","ses.th_blocks":"Blocks","ses.th_seen":"Last seen","ses.th_client":"Client","ses.th_input":"Cum. input","ses.th_folds":"Compressions","ses.empty":"No sessions yet","ses.empty_hint":"The first request through the proxy creates one automatically","ses.count":"{count} sessions","ses.refresh":"Refresh","ses.filter_protocol_tip":"Filter by protocol","ses.filter_client_tip":"Filter by client","ses.filter_state_tip":"Filter by runtime state","ses.filter_all":"All protocols","ses.filter_all_clients":"All clients","ses.filter_state_all":"All states","ses.filter_state_live":"Live","ses.filter_state_history":"History","ses.filter_unknown":"Unknown","ses.reset_filters":"Reset filters","ses.prev_page":"Previous","ses.next_page":"Next","ses.page_label":"Page {page} of {pages}","ses.filtered_count":"{shown} / {total} sessions","data.error":"Failed to load data: {msg} \xB7 auto-retrying with backoff","data.generic":"network error or request timed out","data.timeout":"request timed out (20s)","det.identity":"Identity","det.version":"Proxy version","det.storage_mode":"Storage mode","det.storage_mode_full":"full (unified-first reads, dual-write)","det.storage_mode_shadow":"shadow (dual-write dry-run)","det.storage_mode_legacy":"legacy (json only)","det.active_pack":"Prompt pack","det.conflicts_title":"Compression conflicts","det.conflicts_hint":"Evidence another compressor touched this session (diagnostic, not history)","det.conflicts_more":"{n} earlier event(s)\u2026","det.conflicts_clear":"Clear this session's records","det.conflicts_cleared":"Cleared","det.obudget_degraded":"\u26A0\uFE0F Model {model} has NO known output ceiling: its output budget is raised to {value} tokens (the larger of the client's own estimate and the absolute minimum; no authoritative ceiling to back it), so longer replies may be cut off at the output limit. Declare an output limit for this provider/model in bili config, or set maxTokens on the model in the host profile (#2904/#3071)","det.usage":"Usage","det.last_input":"Last single-turn input","det.upper_bound":"bound {v} (char-count upper bound \u2014 safety protection only, not actual usage)","det.ctx_age":"snap {v} ago","det.ctx_age_tip":"When this context number was measured/estimated; it stops refreshing on restore or idle \u2014 an old snapshot is not the current sent view","det.calib_chip":"k\u0302={k} \xB7 {n} samples \xB7 spread {spread}\xD7 \xB7 {origin}","det.calib_tip":"Calibration factor k\u0302: mean of the last {n} consistent samples (spread {spread}\xD7) on this route+model; deflates estimates only; relearned after a route or model change. Source {origin}{model}.","det.ccr":"CCR content retrieval","det.ccr_detail":"{calls} calls \xB7 {hits} hits \xB7 {misses} misses","det.store":"Content store","det.trajectory":"Context trajectory","det.trajectory_sub":"Per-request input tokens and cache hits; red marks are compression folds","det.trajectory_empty":"No usage samples for this session yet","det.hitrate":"Cache hit rate","det.hitrate_sub":"Per-request hit %; dips colored by ledger attribution (same buckets as the trajectory chart)","det.hitrate_empty":"No cache samples for this session yet","det.legend_hitline":"hit %","det.legend_input":"input","det.legend_cached":"of which cached","det.legend_fold":"compression fold","det.legend_window":"context window limit","det.cause_cold":"cold start (no prior cache)","det.cause_comp":"post-fold rebuild","det.cause_ttl":"unattributed repay \xB7 rest","det.cause_unattrib":"unattributed repay","det.leg_pttl":"\u23F1 upstream TTL expiry","det.leg_pside":"\u25B2 provider-side miss","det.leg_rewind":"\u21A9 rewind","det.leg_client":"\u270E client rewrite","det.leg_rest":"rest","det.fold_short":"fold","det.traj_zoom_hint":"Drag across the chart to zoom into a sample range; double-click or press Esc to reset","det.traj_zoomed":"View #{a}-#{b} ({times})","det.traj_reset":"Reset view","ov.gross_note":"sums each fold's savings across every later request (theoretical upper bound)","ov.net_excl":"pre-tagging sessions without samples not included","det.omitted":"earliest {n} samples were trimmed at write time: each session keeps only its most recent 4096 cache samples (unrecoverable), so the curve starts at the oldest retained sample","ov.saved_neg_tip":"Negative net savings: post-fold rebuild (summary re-read cost) exceeded the theoretical gain; typical of short sessions that ended right after folding","det.cache_econ":"Cache economics","det.ce_new":"New content","det.ce_comp":"Post-fold rebuild","det.ce_comp_hint":"Tip: lowering compress.preserveRecentMessages (the protected recent-message count) reduces this \u2014 minimum 1","det.ce_ttl":"Unattributed repay","det.ce_breakdown":"of which:","det.attr_rest":"rest {x}","det.attr_rest_tip":"small residuals below the classification threshold (<8K or <30% of input per sample), not individually classified","det.ce_residual":"Residual","det.ce_balanced":"Ledger balanced \u2713","det.ce_unbalanced":"Ledger unbalanced \u2717","det.attr_seam":"\u26A0 Cache seam","det.attr_provider":"\u25B2 Provider-side miss (abnormal)","det.attr_ttl":"\u23F1 upstream TTL expiry (normal)","det.attr_ttl_tip":"byte-stable / append-shaped misses settled more than 10 minutes after the previous sample \u2014 the upstream prefix cache simply aged out; expected cost, no action needed","det.attr_rewind":"\u21A9 History rewound","det.attr_client":"\u270E Client mid-history rewrite","det.attr_abort":"\u23FB Abort-correlated","det.attr_seam_tip":"Outbound bodies diverged mid-history with no fold/model-switch/restart attribution \u2014 suspected rebuild seam. Value = tokens re-billed on suspect samples. If a fold landed minutes earlier this is usually the post-fold client-echo re-bill (fold-owned since #2929)","det.attr_provider_tip":"Arrived shortly after the previous request, whose entire message list came back byte-identical (whole body, or its prefix with only tail messages appended; above the 512 KiB forensics cap, proven by the stable recorded head plus exact message-count growth) yet the upstream did not serve its cache \u2014 abnormal: eviction / relay node rotation. Long-gap siblings are booked under upstream TTL expiry","det.attr_rewind_tip":"Client revert/trim shrank the message count \u2014 sanctioned one-time re-bill of the retained prefix, not a defect","det.attr_client_tip":"The client's own resent history diverged mid-list (insert/rewrite \u2014 another host plugin, paste hoisting, re-render): the inbound message-fingerprint pair mismatches at that index, and bili's faithful rebuild carried the change to the wire. Client-owned re-bill, not a bili rebuild seam (#3023)","det.attr_abort_tip":"Missed samples settled within 30s of a client mid-stream abort \u2014 retry churn rewrites the resent tail; correlation, not causation (overlay marker, not a bucket)","det.attr_restart":"\u27F3 restart drop","det.attr_restart_tip":"After a bili restart or session restore the ledger window breaks: the first post-restart request cannot pair with pre-restart samples, so its miss is billed as a first bill (initial content)","det.ledger_gap":"ledger misses {n} reqs","det.ledger_gap_tip":"The hit/miss ledger only covers requests since its last (re)build point; requests outside the window are not counted \u2014 common with multiple instances sharing a state directory. Folds inside the gap are also missing from fold economics","det.seam_events":"\u26A0 Cache-seam events \xB7 {n}","det.seam_events_tip":"First divergence between consecutive outbound bodies; if reproducible attach bili.log around this time (#1548-family)","det.stab_title":"Body Stability (per-call byte proof)","det.stab_pairs":"{n} adjacent pairs","det.stab_tip":"SHA-256 byte comparison of each outbound body against the previous settled request: identical = byte-exact (e.g. transport retry); diverged pairs classified by first divergence \u2014 head <1KiB = host-side parameter change (model/tools/sampling), tail-append = pure tail growth, mid-history = a real prefix rewrite, tail = trailing top-level params or ephemeral tail notes at/past the message-array end (history bytes untouched, cache unaffected), offset-unknown = bodies above the retention cap (inequality still proven by digest)","det.stab_identical":"byte-identical","det.stab_head":"head <1KiB (param change)","det.stab_append":"tail-append","det.stab_mid":"mid-history rewrite","det.stab_tail":"tail (params / ephemeral notes)","det.stab_unknown":"offset unknown (capped)","det.stab_size":"hit% by input size (median)","det.stab_gap":"inter-request gap median: low-hit(<80%) {a}s vs high-hit {b}s","det.seam_col_hit":"hit %","det.seam_col_input":"input","det.seam_col_div":"first divergence","det.seam_msg":"message[{i}] ({prev}\u2192{cur} msgs)","det.seam_mark_tip":"\u26A0 CACHE SEAM #{seq} \xB7 {at} \xB7 hit {hit}% \xB7 first divergence \u2265{lcp} bytes @ message[{msg}] ({prev}\u2192{cur} msgs)","det.legend_seam":"cache seam","det.folds":"Fold breakdown","det.folds_empty":"No fold events yet","det.fold_s":"compressed S","det.fold_sigma":"summary \u03C3","det.fold_h":"post-fold hit %","det.fold_t":"cumulative repay T","det.client_hint":"client","det.self_heal":"Self-heal","det.self_heal_tip":"Stuck-session self-heal has taken over \u2014 see session detail (#2155)","det.self_heal_short":"heal","det.self_heal_degrade_to_proxy":"plugin lane gone \u2192 degraded to proxy mode (tools re-injected)","det.self_heal_suppress_nudge":"nudge idle loop \u2192 suppressed (lifts when compression resumes)","det.auto_mode_forge":"auto-mode verdicts","det.auto_mode_forge_tip":"This session's auto-mode safety verdicts are answered locally by bili \u2014 no upstream model call, zero billing (#2740)","det.auto_mode_forge_short":"forge","det.auto_mode_forge_local":"auto-mode verdicts answered locally by bili (zero upstream traffic)","det.legend_base":"system prompt baseline (measured, not compressible)","det.legend_base_est":"baseline est. (system prompt & tools, not compressible)","det.blocks_title":"Compression blocks","det.blocks_count":"{total} \xB7 {active} active","det.blocks_empty":"No compression blocks yet","det.block_active":"active","det.block_external":"external","det.block_inactive":"inactive","det.blocks_download":"download blocks (.md)","det.report_dl":"download cache report (.md)","det.report_md":"full report \xB7 Markdown","det.report_png":"full report \xB7 image (PNG)","det.report_note":"title & other PII masked by default","det.report_masked":"[masked]","det.rpt_input":"input","det.rpt_cached":"cached","det.rpt_missed":"missed","det.rpt_hit":"hit %","det.blocks_copy_md":"copy Markdown","det.tab_overview":"Overview","det.tab_blocks":"Structure","det.tab_handoff":"Handoff","det.tree_total":"{n} blocks","det.tree_active":"{n} active","det.tree_split":"covered {x} \u2192 summary {y} ({p})","det.tree_msgs":"{n} msgs","det.tree_direct":"{n} direct","det.tree_orig_one":"Original (this level)","det.tree_orig_full":"Original (full)","det.tree_orig_meta":"{n} messages \xB7 {b}","det.tree_orig_truncated":"truncated at {b}","det.tree_orig_missing":"No content snapshot for this block (not kept at fold time, or already pruned)","det.tree_msgs_unavailable":"This block's direct messages are no longer in the session (pruned by native compaction) \u2014 their m-refs cannot be listed","det.tree_msg_gone":"This message is no longer in the session (pruned by native compaction)","det.tree_hint":"Nested by fold parent: T1 folds raw messages, T2 folds T1 blocks, and so on. Original loads the covered bytes on demand.","det.tree_view_list":"List","det.tree_view_graph":"Tree map","det.tree_graph_hint":"Overall shape: each box is one block, top-down is which block folded which. Click a box to jump to that row in the list.","det.tree_graph_legend":"solid border = active, dashed = archived","det.handoff":"Handoff document","det.handoff_hint":"Same content as bili export \u2014 paste into a new session to continue","det.thinking":"thinking","det.handoff_truncated":"\u26A0\uFE0F Content truncated for display","det.handoff_copy_md":"Copy as Markdown","det.handoff_download":"Download .md","det.not_found":"Session not found","det.not_found_hint":"It may have been deleted or lives outside this data dir","cfg.title":"Configuration","cfg.sub":"Edits write straight to the config file and hot-apply \xB7 check JSON syntax before saving","cfg.file":"Config file","cfg.parse_error":"Config file is not valid JSON \u2014 showing an empty view","cfg.relay_warn":"The draft enables security.adminRelay (admin relay): anyone who can reach the dsh web entry gets the FULL bili admin panel through it \u2014 including config edits and credential writes. Make sure that entry is behind login auth or a reverse proxy; remove the field to turn it back off.","cfg.upstream_net":"Upstream network","cfg.up_auto":"auto (follow system proxy)","cfg.up_manual":"manual (explicit proxy)","cfg.up_direct":"direct (force direct)","cfg.passthrough":"Passthrough","cfg.passthrough_desc":"Decides whether traffic matching no route passes through to the target service untouched (no interception, n